text: ['All creatures able to block Elvish Bard do so.', "An opponent chooses one —\\n• You draw three cards at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.\\n• You search your library for a card, put that card into your hand, then shuffle.", "An opponent chooses one —\\n• You draw three cards.\\n• You destroy up to two target creatures that player controls. They can't be regenerated. That player draws up to three cards.", 'An opponent chooses one —\\n• You put a +1/+1 counter on each creature you control and gain 4 life.\\n• You put a -1/-1 counter on each creature that player controls and Misfortune deals 4 damage to that player.', 'As Sol Grail enters the battlefield, choose a color.\\n{T}: Add one mana of the chosen color.', "As an additional cost to cast this spell, discard a red or green card.\\nTarget creature gains trample and gets +X/+0 until end of turn, where X is that creature's mana value.", 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice a creature.\\nGain control of target nonartifact, nonblack creature.', 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, you may pay {1}{G} any number of times.\\nYou gain 3 life plus an additional 3 life for each additional {1}{G} you paid.', 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, you may pay {1}{R} and/or {1}{G} any number of times.\\nDestroy target artifact. For each additional {1}{R} you paid, destroy another target artifact. For each additional {1}{G} you paid, destroy another target artifact, and you gain 1 life.', "As an additional cost to cast this spell, you may pay {2}{R}.\\nPrevent all combat damage that would be dealt this turn. If this spell's additional cost was paid, this effect doesn't affect combat damage that would be dealt by red creatures.", 'As long as Juniper Order Advocate is untapped, green creatures you control get +1/+1.', 'At end of combat, if Kjeldoran Home Guard attacked or blocked this combat, put a -0/-1 counter on Kjeldoran Home Guard and create a 0/1 white Deserter creature token.', 'At the beginning of the end step, if Krovikan Horror is in your graveyard with a creature card directly above it, you may return Krovikan Horror to your hand.\\n{1}, Sacrifice a creature: Krovikan Horror deals 1 damage to any target.', "At the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice Nature's Wrath unless you pay {G}.\\nWhenever a player puts an Island or blue permanent onto the battlefield, that player sacrifices an Island or blue permanent.\\nWhenever a player puts a Swamp or black permanent onto the battlefield, that player sacrifices a Swamp or black permanent.", "At the beginning of your upkeep, you may sacrifice a Forest. If you sacrifice a snow Forest this way, Gargantuan Gorilla gains trample until end of turn. If you don't sacrifice a Forest, sacrifice Gargantuan Gorilla and it deals 7 damage to you.\\n{T}: Gargantuan Gorilla deals damage equal to its power to another target creature. That creature deals damage equal to its power to Gargantuan Gorilla.", "Banding (Any creatures with banding, and up to one without, can attack in a band. Bands are blocked as a group. If any creatures with banding you control are blocking or being blocked by a creature, you divide that creature's combat damage, not its controller, among any of the creatures it's being blocked by or is blocking.)", "Cast this spell only during combat before blockers are declared.\\nAll creatures gain menace until end of turn. (They can't be blocked except by two or more creatures.)\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", "Cast this spell only if you were dealt damage this turn by a red instant or sorcery spell.\\nSuffocation deals 4 damage to the controller of the last red instant or sorcery spell that dealt damage to you this turn.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", "Choose one —\\n• Create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token.\\n• Destroy target nonartifact, nonblack creature. It can't be regenerated.", "Counter target instant spell if it's blue.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", "Counter target spell. Its controller may draw up to two cards at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.\\nYou draw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", "Create a 1/1 white Knight creature token with banding. (Any creatures with banding, and up to one without, can attack in a band. Bands are blocked as a group. If any creatures with banding you control are blocking or being blocked by a creature, you divide that creature's combat damage, not its controller, among any of the creatures it's being blocked by or is blocking.)", 'Cumulative upkeep {1}{W} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nDamage that would reduce your life total to less than 1 reduces it to 1 instead.', 'Cumulative upkeep {2} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nPay 2 life or {2}: Counter target red or green spell. Any player may activate this ability.', 'Cumulative upkeep {G} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\n{2}{G}, Pay 3 life for each velocity counter on Tornado: Destroy target permanent and put a velocity counter on Tornado. Activate only once each turn.', "Cumulative upkeep {W} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nWhenever a Swamp, Mountain, black permanent, or red permanent becomes tapped, Royal Decree deals 1 damage to that permanent's controller.", "Cumulative upkeep—Exile the top card of your library. (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nWhen a player doesn't pay Thought Lash's cumulative upkeep, that player exiles all cards from their library.\\nExile the top card of your library: Prevent the next 1 damage that would be dealt to you this turn.", 'Cumulative upkeep—Have an opponent create a 1/1 red Survivor creature token. (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nTrample; rampage 1 (Whenever this creature becomes blocked, it gets +1/+1 until end of turn for each creature blocking it beyond the first.)', "Cumulative upkeep—Pay 1 life. (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)\\nAt the beginning of each player's upkeep, that player sacrifices a green or white permanent.", 'Death Spark deals 1 damage to any target.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, if Death Spark is in your graveyard with a creature card directly above it, you may pay {1}. If you do, return Death Spark to your hand.', "Defender; reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)\\nYou may choose not to untap Whip Vine during your untap step.\\n{T}: Tap target creature with flying blocked by Whip Vine. That creature doesn't untap during its controller's untap step for as long as Whip Vine remains tapped.", 'Defender\\nWhenever Shield Sphere blocks, put a -0/-1 counter on it.', "Destroy target artifact or land. It can't be regenerated.", "Destroy target creature with power 4 or greater. It can't be regenerated.", "Each player may play an additional land during each of their turns.\\nWhenever a land is tapped for mana, return it to its owner's hand.", 'Each player shuffles their hand and graveyard into their library. You exile the top ten cards of your library. Then each player draws up to seven cards.', 'Enchant creature you control\\nTap enchanted creature: Target creature other than the creature tapped this way gets +2/+1 until end of turn. Activate only if enchanted creature is untapped.', 'Enchant creature you control\\n{0}: Untap enchanted creature. Activate only during your turn and only once each turn.\\nTap enchanted creature: Untap target artifact, creature, or land. Activate only if enchanted creature is white and untapped and only once each turn.', "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can't be blocked unless defending player pays {3} for each creature they control that's blocking it.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+1.\\n{1}{U}: Return Viscerid Armor to its owner's hand.", 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+2.\\n{2}{U}: Attach Kjeldoran Pride to target creature other than enchanted creature.', "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+1 as long as it's black. Otherwise, it gets -1/-2.", "Enchant creature\\nWhen Bestial Fury enters the battlefield, draw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.\\nWhenever enchanted creature becomes blocked, it gets +4/+0 and gains trample until end of turn.", 'Enchant creature\\nWhen enchanted creature dies, draw three cards, then discard one of them.', 'Enchant creature\\nWhen enchanted creature dies, return that card to the battlefield under your control.', 'Enchant creature\\nWhenever enchanted creature blocks or becomes blocked, it gets +0/+3 until end of turn and you gain 1 life.', "Enchant non-Wall creature you control\\nWhen Krovikan Plague enters the battlefield, draw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.\\nTap enchanted creature: Krovikan Plague deals 1 damage to any target. Put a -0/-1 counter on enchanted creature. Activate only if enchanted creature is untapped.", 'Exile Elvish Spirit Guide from your hand: Add {G}.', 'Exile target nonwhite attacking creature. You gain life equal to its toughness.', "First strike\\n{1}{B}: Regenerate Lim-Dûl's High Guard.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)", 'Flying, first strike\\n{W}{W}: Wild Aesthir gets +2/+0 until end of turn. Activate only once each turn.', "Flying\\nAesthir Glider can't block.", 'Flying\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, put a +1/+1 counter on Phantasmal Sphere, then sacrifice Phantasmal Sphere unless you pay {1} for each +1/+1 counter on it.\\nWhen Phantasmal Sphere leaves the battlefield, target opponent creates an X/X blue Orb creature token with flying, where X is the number of +1/+1 counters on Phantasmal Sphere.', "Flying\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, put a wage counter on Rogue Skycaptain. You may pay {2} for each wage counter on it. If you don't, remove all wage counters from Rogue Skycaptain and an opponent gains control of it.", "Flying\\nWhen Carrier Pigeons enters the battlefield, draw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", "Flying\\nWhen Ivory Gargoyle dies, return it to the battlefield under its owner's control at the beginning of the next end step and you skip your next draw step.\\n{4}{W}: Exile Ivory Gargoyle.", "Flying\\nWhenever Swamp Mosquito attacks and isn't blocked, defending player gets a poison counter. (A player with ten or more poison counters loses the game.)", 'Flying\\n{U}, Exile the top card of your library: Tap target creature with flying.\\n{U}, Exile the top card of your library: If the exiled card is a snow land, Storm Elemental gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Green creatures you control get +1/+1.', 'Guerrilla Tactics deals 2 damage to any target.\\nWhen a spell or ability an opponent controls causes you to discard Guerrilla Tactics, Guerrilla Tactics deals 4 damage to any target.', 'Hail Storm deals 2 damage to each attacking creature and 1 damage to you and each creature you control.', 'Haste\\nRampage 1 (Whenever this creature becomes blocked, it gets +1/+1 until end of turn for each creature blocking it beyond the first.)', "If Balduvian Trading Post would enter the battlefield, sacrifice an untapped Mountain instead. If you do, put Balduvian Trading Post onto the battlefield. If you don't, put it into its owner's graveyard.\\n{T}: Add {C}{R}.\\n{1}, {T}: Balduvian Trading Post deals 1 damage to target attacking creature.", "If Heart of Yavimaya would enter the battlefield, sacrifice a Forest instead. If you do, put Heart of Yavimaya onto the battlefield. If you don't, put it into its owner's graveyard.\\n{T}: Add {G}.\\n{T}: Target creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.", "If Kjeldoran Outpost would enter the battlefield, sacrifice a Plains instead. If you do, put Kjeldoran Outpost onto the battlefield. If you don't, put it into its owner's graveyard.\\n{T}: Add {W}.\\n{1}{W}, {T}: Create a 1/1 white Soldier creature token.", "If Lake of the Dead would enter the battlefield, sacrifice a Swamp instead. If you do, put Lake of the Dead onto the battlefield. If you don't, put it into its owner's graveyard.\\n{T}: Add {B}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice a Swamp: Add {B}{B}{B}{B}.", 'If Sheltered Valley would enter the battlefield, instead sacrifice each other permanent named Sheltered Valley you control, then put Sheltered Valley onto the battlefield.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, if you control three or fewer lands, you gain 1 life.\\n{T}: Add {C}.', "If Soldevi Excavations would enter the battlefield, sacrifice an untapped Island instead. If you do, put Soldevi Excavations onto the battlefield. If you don't, put it into its owner's graveyard.\\n{T}: Add {C}{U}.\\n{1}, {T}: Scry 1.", 'Look at the top five cards of your library. As many times as you choose, you may pay 1 life, put those cards on the bottom of your library in any order, then look at the top five cards of your library. Then shuffle and put the last cards you looked at this way on top in any order.', 'Nonartifact creatures get -1/-1 until end of turn.', "Put up to three target cards from an opponent's graveyard on top of their library in any order.", 'Put up to three target creature cards from your graveyard on top of your library.', "Return all Islands to their owners' hands. Each player sacrifices a Plains or a white permanent for each white permanent they control.", "Search your library for three cards, exile them, then shuffle.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", "Shroud (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities.)", "Shuffle a card from your hand into your library. If you do, draw two cards at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", "Target creature gets +2/+0 until end of turn.\\nDraw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", "Thawing Glaciers enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{1}, {T}: Search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle. Return Thawing Glaciers to its owner's hand at the beginning of the next cleanup step.", 'Trample, haste\\nCumulative upkeep {G}{G} (At the beginning of your upkeep, put an age counter on this permanent, then sacrifice it unless you pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)', "Trample; rampage 2 (Whenever this creature becomes blocked, it gets +2/+2 until end of turn for each creature blocking it beyond the first.)\\nGorilla Berserkers can't be blocked except by three or more creatures.", "Trample\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you may discard a card. If you don't, sacrifice Lim-Dûl's Paladin and draw a card.\\nWhenever Lim-Dûl's Paladin becomes blocked, it gets +6/+3 until end of turn.\\nWhenever Lim-Dûl's Paladin attacks and isn't blocked, it assigns no combat damage this turn and defending player loses 4 life.", "Trample\\n{3}: Urza's Engine gains banding until end of turn. (Any creatures with banding, and up to one without, can attack in a band. Bands are blocked as a group. If any creatures with banding you control are blocking or being blocked by a creature, you divide that creature's combat damage, not its controller, among any of the creatures it's being blocked by or is blocking.)\\n{3}: Attacking creatures banded with Urza's Engine gain trample until end of turn.", 'Untap any number of target creatures. Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt to and dealt by those creatures this turn.', 'Until end of turn, target creature you control gains "{0}: The next 1 damage that would be dealt to target creature, planeswalker, or player this turn is dealt to this creature instead." Only you may activate this ability.', 'When Balduvian Horde enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless you discard a card at random.', 'When Fyndhorn Druid dies, if it was blocked this turn, you gain 4 life.', 'When Insidious Bookworms dies, you may pay {1}{B}. If you do, target player discards a card at random.', 'When Lord of Tresserhorn enters the battlefield, you lose 2 life, you sacrifice two creatures, and target opponent draws two cards.\\n{B}: Regenerate Lord of Tresserhorn.', "When Phyrexian Devourer's power is 7 or greater, sacrifice it.\\nExile the top card of your library: Put X +1/+1 counters on Phyrexian Devourer, where X is the exiled card's mana value.", 'When Phyrexian War Beast leaves the battlefield, sacrifice a land and Phyrexian War Beast deals 1 damage to you.', 'Whenever Diseased Vermin deals combat damage to a player, put an infection counter on it.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, Diseased Vermin deals X damage to target opponent previously dealt damage by it, where X is the number of infection counters on it.', "Whenever Keeper of Tresserhorn attacks and isn't blocked, it assigns no combat damage this turn and defending player loses 2 life.", 'Whenever Soldevi Steam Beast becomes tapped, target opponent gains 2 life.\\n{2}: Regenerate Soldevi Steam Beast.', "Whenever Stromgald Spy attacks and isn't blocked, you may have defending player play with their hand revealed for as long as Stromgald Spy remains on the battlefield. If you do, Stromgald Spy assigns no combat damage this turn.", 'Whenever a creature dies, you may pay {3}. If you do, draw a card.', "Whenever a player taps a snow land for mana, that player adds one mana of any type that land produced. That land doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.", "You may exile a green card from your hand rather than pay this spell's mana cost.\\nDistribute three +1/+1 counters among one, two, or three target creatures. For each +1/+1 counter you put on a creature this way, remove a +1/+1 counter from that creature at the beginning of the next cleanup step.", "You may exile a red card from your hand rather than pay this spell's mana cost.\\nPyrokinesis deals 4 damage divided as you choose among any number of target creatures.", "You may exile a white card from your hand rather than pay this spell's mana cost.\\nPrevent the next 7 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn. If it's a creature, put a +0/+1 counter on it for each 1 damage prevented this way at the beginning of the next end step.", "You may pay 1 life and exile a black card from your hand rather than pay this spell's mana cost.\\nDistribute two -2/-1 counters among one or two target creatures.", "You may pay 1 life and exile a blue card from your hand rather than pay this spell's mana cost.\\nCounter target spell.", "{0}: Varchild's Crusader can't be blocked this turn except by Walls. Sacrifice Varchild's Crusader at the beginning of the next end step.", "{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Astrolabe: Add two mana of any one color. Draw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", "{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Lodestone Bauble: Put up to four target basic land cards from a player's graveyard on top of their library in any order. That player draws a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", '{1}, {T}: Target land becomes the basic land type of your choice until end of turn.', '{1}: Choose target opponent. Regenerate Soldevi Sentry. When it regenerates this way, that player may draw a card.', "{1}: Sworn Defender's power becomes the toughness of target creature blocking or being blocked by Sworn Defender minus 1 until end of turn, and Sworn Defender's toughness becomes 1 plus the power of that creature until end of turn.", '{1}{G}: Regenerate Gorilla Chieftain.', '{1}{W}: Target creature gains first strike until end of turn.', '{1}{W}: Target nonattacking, nonblocking creature gets +0/+2 until end of turn.', '{2}, Exile the top card of your library: You gain 1 life.', '{2}, Exile the top two cards of your library: Whirling Catapult deals 1 damage to each creature with flying and each player.', "{2}: Enslaved Scout gains mountainwalk until end of turn. (It can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Mountain.)", '{2}: Put the top card of your graveyard on the bottom of your library.', '{2}{G}: Splintering Wind deals 1 damage to target creature. Create a 1/1 green Splinter creature token. It has flying and "Cumulative upkeep {G}." When it leaves the battlefield, it deals 1 damage to you and each creature you control. (At the beginning of its controller\'s upkeep, that player puts an age counter on it, then sacrifices it unless they pay its upkeep cost for each age counter on it.)', '{2}{R}, Exile a creature card from your graveyard: Create a 3/1 black and red Graveborn creature token with haste. Sacrifice it at the beginning of the next end step.', '{2}{U}{U}: Look at the top five cards of your library, put one of them into your hand, and exile the rest.', '{3}, Exile the top four cards of your library: The next time a source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage.', '{3}, {T}: Target player looks at the top three cards of their library, puts one of them back on top of their library, then exiles the rest.', '{3}: If your library has ten or more cards in it, target opponent looks at the top ten cards of your library and separates them into two face-down piles. Exile one of those piles. Search the other pile for a card, put it into your hand, then shuffle the rest of that pile into your library.', "{B}: Phantasmal Fiend gets +1/-1 until end of turn.\\n{1}{U}: Switch Phantasmal Fiend's power and toughness until end of turn.", "{G}: Phelddagrif gains trample until end of turn. Target opponent creates a 1/1 green Hippo creature token.\\n{W}: Phelddagrif gains flying until end of turn. Target opponent gains 2 life.\\n{U}: Return Phelddagrif to its owner's hand. Target opponent may draw a card.", '{G}: Yavimaya Ancients gets +1/-2 until end of turn.', "{G}{W}, Discard a card: Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature or that creature gains banding, first strike, or trample. (This effect lasts indefinitely. Any creatures with banding, and up to one without, can attack in a band. Bands are blocked as a group. If any creatures with banding a player controls are blocking or being blocked by a creature, that player divides that creature's combat damage, not its controller, among any of the creatures it's being blocked by or is blocking.)", '{R}, {T}: Target player shuffles their library.', '{R}: Add {B}.', '{R}: Exile the top card of your library. If that card is a land card, Chaos Harlequin gets -4/-0 until end of turn. Otherwise, Chaos Harlequin gets +2/+0 until end of turn.', '{R}: Storm Shaman gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', "{T}, Sacrifice Mishra's Groundbreaker: Target land becomes a 3/3 artifact creature that's still a land. (This effect lasts indefinitely.)", "{T}, Sacrifice Scarab of the Unseen: Return all Auras attached to target permanent you own to their owners' hands. Draw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", "{T}, Sacrifice a black or artifact creature: Add an amount of {B} equal to the sacrificed creature's mana value.", "{T}, Sacrifice a creature and a Swamp: Destroy target nonartifact creature. It can't be regenerated.\\n{T}, Sacrifice a creature and a snow Swamp: Destroy target creature. It can't be regenerated.", '{T}, Sacrifice two lands: Draw three cards, then discard one of them.', '{T}, Untap a tapped land an opponent controls: Add one mana of any type that land could produce.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}, {T}: Add one mana of any color.', "{T}: Exile a card from your hand face down. You may look at it for as long as it remains exiled.\\n{T}: Return a card you own exiled with Gustha's Scepter to your hand.\\nWhen you lose control of Gustha's Scepter, put all cards exiled with Gustha's Scepter into their owner's graveyard.", '{U}: Regenerate Spiny Starfish.\\nAt the beginning of each end step, if Spiny Starfish regenerated this turn, create a 0/1 blue Starfish creature token for each time it regenerated this turn.', '{W}, Pay 1 life: Prevent the next 2 damage that would be dealt to target creature this turn.\\n{U}: Prevent the next 1 damage that would be dealt to target Cleric or Wizard creature this turn.\\n{B}, Put a -1/-1 counter on a creature you control: Prevent the next 2 damage that would be dealt to target player or planeswalker this turn.', '{W}, {T}: Prevent the next 2 damage that would be dealt to target creature this turn. Target opponent may draw a card.', "{X}, {T}: Target opponent mills a card, then repeats this process until a creature card or X cards have been put into their graveyard this way, whichever comes first. If one or more creature cards were put into that graveyard this way, sacrifice Helm of Obedience and put one of them onto the battlefield under your control. X can't be 0.", '{X}{X}{1}, {T}: Tap X target lands.', '{X}{X}{1}: Destroy target noncreature artifact with mana value X.']
flavor: ['"A dreadful invention. What ease is there under the watchful eye of cold steel?"\\n—Sorine Relicbane, Soldevi Heretic', '"A fine example of the rewards of artifice: a thoroughly obedient steed with wings of Soldevi steel."\\n—Arcum Dagsson, Soldevi Machinist', '"All knowledge has its price."\\n—Gerda Äagesdotter, Archmage of the Unseen', '"All struggles ultimately require sacrifice. It\'s just that some sacrifices are dearer than others."\\n—Jaeuhl Carthalion, Juniper Order Advocate', '"All the knowledge of Lat-Nam could not protect its sages from the Brothers\' War."\\n—Gerda Äagesdotter, Archmage of the Unseen', '"An idiot cannot hear sense, even when a thousand people speak it."\\n—Sorine Relicbane, Soldevi Heretic', '"And *I* say north is where I *want* it to be!"\\n—Jaya Ballard, Task Mage', '"Any who drink of Freyalise\'s bounty drink the mead of rebirth."\\n—Kaysa, Elder Druid of the Juniper Order', '"Anybody want some . . . *toast*?"\\n—Jaya Ballard, Task Mage', '"At the core of all power is raw passion." —Gerda Äagesdotter, Archmage of the Unseen', '"Be open to the blessings, whatever their form."\\n—Kaysa, Elder Druid of the Juniper Order', '"Beautiful, indeed—but one sting could fell a Giant in a heartbeat."\\n—Taaveti of Kelsinko, Elvish Hunter', '"Beneath serenity may lie a hidden rage."\\n—Jaeuhl Carthalion, Juniper Order Advocate', '"Birds know no borders! Why, then, should we?"\\n—General Varchild, in a missive to King Darien of Kjeldor', '"Call every able sword to our side. Kjeldor will stand triumphant!"\\n—King Darien of Kjeldor', '"Dagsson saw the steam as life-giving—until his followers felt its scalding touch."\\n—Sorine Relicbane, Soldevi Heretic', '"Dagsson should have paid attention to the lessons of Phyrexia before attempting to create a mechanical utopia."\\n—Sorine Relicbane, Soldevi Heretic', '"Deal with the spawn of Phyrexia cautiously; only with time may we control them."\\n—Arcum Dagsson, Soldevi Machinist', '"Death does not prevent us from service to our absent master. As long as Tresserhorn stands, so shall we."\\n—Chaeska, Keeper of Tresserhorn', '"Direct confrontation never was to the Orcs\' taste."\\n—General Varchild', '"Disa is dead, and I am left. I shall allow no others to succumb to this pestilence."\\n—Kolbjörn, High Honored Druid', '"Each generation teaches the next that artifice is the enemy of natural order."\\n—Kaysa, Elder Druid of the Juniper Order', '"Embrace the storm. Its voice shall echo within you, and its fire shall become your touch!"\\n—Lovisa Coldeyes,\\nBalduvian Chieftain', '"Even the basest creatures may serve a purpose. Still, their lives need be only as long as the paths we tread."\\n—General Varchild', '"Every patch of land must belong to Kjeldor, no matter what the cost!"\\n—General Varchild', '"Faith is our greatest protector."\\n—Halvor Arensson, Kjeldoran Priest', '"Far too many of our missing \'dead\' seem to be turning up in Varchild\'s ranks!"\\n—King Darien of Kjeldor', '"Few natural forces are as devastating as hunger."\\n—Kaysa, Elder Druid of the Juniper Order', '"Fool! Never believe they\'re dead until you see the body!"\\n—General Varchild', '"Frankly, destruction is best left to professionals."\\n—Jaya Ballard, Task Mage', '"GOTCHA!"\\n—Jaya Ballard, Task Mage', '"Good soldiers rely first upon their training, then upon their instincts."\\n—King Darien of Kjeldor', '"Her soldiers\' hatred for the Goblins is tempered only by their need for what the Goblins alone hold: knowledge of their mountain home."\\n—King Darien of Kjeldor', '"High in the Karplusans, death is swift and razor-clawed."\\n—Arna Kennerüd, Skycaptain', '"Honor those who honor Fyndhorn above themselves."\\n—Kolbjörn, High Honored Druid', '"How can any Human hope to match our skills? We are children of Fyndhorn, and its sap runs in our veins."\\n—Taaveti of Kelsinko, Elvish Hunter', '"Humans and machines working together can be fearsome indeed!"\\n—Arcum Dagsson', '"I shape my weapons from the fears of my enemies."\\n—Chaeska, Keeper of Tresserhorn', '"If they can\'t take the hail, they\'d better stay home."\\n—Arna Kennerüd, Skycaptain', '"In the arms of tragedy, there is little comfort in being right."\\n—Sorine Relicbane, Soldevi Heretic', '"In the soil of leadership sprout the seeds of immortality."\\n—Kaysa, Elder Druid of the Juniper Order', '"In these troubled times, we alone carry the hope of reconciliation between Elf and Human."\\n—Jaeuhl Carthalion, Juniper Order Advocate', '"It cannot be! Soldev crushed, and my machines to blame?"\\n—Arcum Dagsson, Soldevi Machinist', '"It is the work of sorcery. Burn it!"\\n—Taaveti of Kelsinko, Elvish Hunter', '"It tells you that the worst is coming. Do you listen?"\\n—Lovisa Coldeyes, Balduvian Chieftain', '"It\'s not so easy anymore. Nothing grows in Kjeldor but seaweed."\\n—Halvor Arensson, Kjeldoran Priest', '"It\'s true I ask no fealty of the flocks—but surely we are more than mere beasts."\\n—King Darien of Kjeldor, in a missive to General Varchild', '"Just as an Herbalist heals a wound, so must we heal the rift between Balduvia and Kjeldor."\\n—King Darien of Kjeldor', '"Kjeldor\'s borders are secure, and its citizens are prepared to take up arms in defense of their families."\\n—King Darien of Kjeldor', '"Knowing its origins, how could they have thought they could control it?"\\n—Sorine Relicbane, Soldevi Heretic', '"Lat-Nam has bequeathed us its secrets. With them we shall attain true enlightenment."\\n—Gerda Äagesdotter, Archmage of the Unseen', '"Let Balduvia burn to warm Kjeldor\'s hearth!"\\n—General Varchild', '"Let the lightning be your warning, and the thunder your battle cry."\\n—Lovisa Coldeyes, Balduvian Chieftain', '"Let them send their legions! I will show them that my truth is stronger than their swords."\\n—General Varchild', '"Look deep into the Grail, and see there what you desire most."\\n—Gerda Äagesdotter, Archmage of the Unseen', '"Loyalty to coin alone is loyalty nonetheless."\\n—General Varchild', '"Martyrs are cheaper than mercenaries, and a far better investment."\\n—General Varchild', '"May they speed to their task, for the Skyknights alone cannot hold Kjeldor safe."\\n—Arna Kennerüd, Skycaptain', '"More than lessons may be gained from the past."\\n—Halvor Arensson, Kjeldoran Priest', '"My Soldiers know that they need never fear for their protection."\\n—King Darien of Kjeldor', '"My lord, there is only so much I can do. This plague infests Krov worse than any other city."\\n—Halvor Arensson, Kjeldoran Priest', '"No one may fault an Elvish Ranger\'s heart, but the simplest frailty may fell even the proudest warrior."\\n—Kaysa, Elder Druid of the Juniper Order', '"Nothing has ever broken my heart so much as this—the betrayal of Soldev by my beloved machines!"\\n—Arcum Dagsson, Soldevi Machinist', '"Oh, no—not *you* again?!"\\n—Jaya Ballard, Task Mage', '"Once great literature—now great litter."\\n—Jaya Ballard, Task Mage', '"Only a necromancer would create such a foul form of divination."\\n—Gerda Äagesdotter, Archmage of the Unseen', '"Only an animal born in the wild has sufficient heart to be a true Knight\'s steed."\\n—King Darien of Kjeldor', '"Our newfound security enables us to turn more of our attentions to the wonders that lie deep within the soil."\\n—Arcum Dagsson, Soldevi Machinist', '"Our underground archives grow daily, as our excavators and sages alike dig to uncover hidden wonders."\\n—Arcum Dagsson, Soldevi Machinist', '"Peace will come only when we have taken Varchild\'s head."\\n—Lovisa Coldeyes, Balduvian Chieftain', '"People love to follow fools; they don\'t feel so alone then."\\n—Sorine Relicbane, Soldevi Heretic', '"Phyrexia\'s touch is painful to all but the blackest of hearts."\\n—Gerda Äagesdotter, Archmage of the Unseen', '"Relent, and you may transcend your situation."\\n—Gerda Äagesdotter, Archmage of the Unseen', '"Rumors persist of dark deeds performed in the depths of Soldev. When will Dagsson heed the danger therein?"\\n—Sorine Relicbane, Soldevi Heretic', '"Sacrilege! A noble ally in life, made nothing more than a glorified kite in death!"\\n—Arna Kennerüd, Skycaptain', '"Strange alliances are alliances still, and provide the same protection."\\n—King Darien of Kjeldor', '"Teach by example. If your students do not survive, they were not worth the lesson."\\n—General Varchild', '"The \'fabled\' Order of Stromgald is cast to the four winds, lost for all time. I, for one, give them no thought."\\n—General Varchild', '"The Ancients teach us that if we can but last, we shall prevail."\\n—Kaysa, Elder Druid of the Juniper Order', '"The Guard will forever stand ready. For them, death is merely an inconvenience, not an ending."\\n—Chaeska, Keeper of Tresserhorn', '"The Order of Stromgald spreads its poisonous lies from within Varchild\'s troops, and still she sees only visions of conquest."\\n—Lovisa Coldeyes, Balduvian Chieftain', '"The art of war is turning obstacle to advantage."\\n—Jaeuhl Carthalion, Juniper Order Advocate', '"The benefits of peace far outweigh the pride of Generals."\\n—King Darien of Kjeldor', '"The burst of strength brought on by this plague should not be mistaken for a sign of renewed health."\\n—Kolbjörn, High Honored Druid', '"The fever clouds the mind as it energizes the body. Both will pass in time."\\n—Halvor Arensson, Kjeldoran Priest', '"The first caravan has passed safely through the Karplusan Mountains without incident, forging a trade route to Balduvia. Kjeld himself would never have believed it!"\\n—King Darien of Kjeldor', '"The living cannot understand the benefits of death."\\n—Chaeska, Keeper of Tresserhorn', '"The meek shall fight as one, and they shall overcome even the greatest of foes."\\n—Halvor Arensson, Kjeldoran Priest', '"The only \'art\' these beasts possess is the art of noise!"\\n—Jaya Ballard', '"The only true immortality is in dying for a cause."\\n—Halvor Arensson, Kjeldoran Priest', '"Their fury is their greatest weapon."\\n—Taaveti of Kelsinko, Elvish Hunter', '"Theirs is the art of blood."\\n—Jaeuhl Carthalion, Juniper Order Advocate', '"There is no time for pain when this beast leaves its terrible sting."\\n—Jaeuhl Carthalion, Juniper Order Advocate', '"There is, in each of us, the potential to heal and the gift of renewed life."\\n—Kaysa, Elder Druid of the Juniper Order', '"They are fighters as fine as any Knight they carry."\\n—Arna Kennerüd, Skycaptain', '"This ceaseless device has helped uncover marvels unreachable by mere flesh."\\n—Arcum Dagsson, Soldevi Machinist', '"Those mewling Barbarians will cower before my righteous steel!"\\n—General Varchild', '"To hide the truth is more than folly—it is fatal."\\n—Sorine Relicbane, Soldevi Heretic', '"Watch for it! Right on its tailfeathers will be a storm from your nightmares."\\n—Arna Kennerüd, Skycaptain', '"We aided the Balduvians once before. They need but ask and we shall do so again."\\n—King Darien of Kjeldor', '"We are never without guidance, if we but seek it."\\n—Taaveti of Kelsinko, Elvish Hunter', '"We are not yet free of Lim-Dûl\'s terrors."\\n—Halvor Arensson, Kjeldoran Priest', '"We could have peace, but Varchild would rather have the maps of the new Kjeldor drawn in Balduvian blood."\\n—King Darien of Kjeldor', '"We orphans of Fyndhorn have found no welcome in this alien place."\\n—Taaveti of Kelsinko, Elvish Hunter', '"We send our best to battle, but every man, woman, and child will stand against Varchild\'s butchers."\\n—Lovisa Coldeyes, Balduvian Chieftain', '"We willingly trade with Kjeldor, but the peace we build must come from both our lands."\\n—Lovisa Coldeyes, Balduvian Chieftain', '"Were they to reduce us to ash, we would clog their throats and sting their eyes in payment."\\n—Lovisa Coldeyes, Balduvian Chieftain', '"What Barbarian secrets do they spy from their lofty perch?"\\n—General Varchild', '"What tries to crush our spirit only strengthens our resolve."\\n—Lovisa Coldeyes, Balduvian Chieftain', '"When you cannot rely on your sources, trust your own senses. When you cannot trust those, you must follow your instincts."\\n—Lovisa Coldeyes, Balduvian Chieftain', '"Whether whole or not, still we serve Lim-Dûl\'s wishes."\\n—Chaeska, Keeper of Tresserhorn', "A fallen Viscerid's only tribute is to be worn by a comrade.", 'After the terrible retribution visited upon Lat-Nam, this school of mages chose to hide from the eyes of the world.', 'Distant Atlantis charged these Explorers with the task of venturing into unknown waters to track the despised Viscerids.', "Few remember that Ashnod's defilement of Terisiare's resources outstripped even that of her peers.", 'Kaysa speaks as the Elder Druid, but the Yavimaya recognizes only one voice: its own.', "Not all of Terisiare's flooding was natural . . . .", "One Viscerid's death is often another's gain.", 'The rising oceans brought new lakes—and new terrors—to Terisiare. The Explorers found their ancient enemies spawning everywhere.', "The very ground yielded to Mishra's wishes.", 'Viscerid dams may be of living creatures as well as bones and mud.']
artist: ['Alan Rabinowitz', 'Allen Williams', 'Amy Weber', 'Andi Rusu', 'Anson Maddocks', 'Anthony S. Waters', 'Bill Sienkiewicz', 'Brian Snõddy', 'Bryon Wackwitz', 'Carol Heyer', 'Christopher Rush', 'D. Alexander Gregory', 'Dan Frazier', 'Diana Vick', 'Douglas Shuler', 'Greg Simanson', 'Heather Hudson', 'Jeff A. Menges', 'John Matson', 'Julie Baroh', 'Kaja Foglio', 'Lawrence Snelly', 'Liz Danforth', 'Mark Poole', 'Mark Tedin', 'Mike Kimble', 'Mike Raabe', 'Nicola Leonard', 'Pat Lewis', 'Pete Venters', 'Phil Foglio', 'Quinton Hoover', 'Randy Asplund-Faith', 'Randy Gallegos', 'Rebecca Guay', 'Richard Kane Ferguson', 'Rob Alexander', 'Ron Spencer', 'Ruth Thompson', 'Sandra Everingham', 'Scott Kirschner', 'Susan Van Camp', 'Terese Nielsen', 'Tom Wänerstrand', 'Zak Plucinski', 'Zak Plucinski & D. Alexander Gregory']
